# Reading the result:
# - mean_sybil_net > 0 → attack profitable, B_dep too low
# - mean_sybil_net < 0 → deposit forfeitures exceed premiums
# - attack_profitable_rate: fraction of trials with sybilNet > 0
# - commons_deficit: under-compensation suffered by commons when sybil wins

# Closed-form check (single-class, expected-value):
#   B_dep* = q* · (1 − P_loss) / P_loss
#   low-risk  (P=0.05, q*≈1):    B_dep* ≈ 19.0
#   med-risk  (P=0.10, q*≈10):   B_dep* ≈ 90.0
#   high-risk (P=0.20, q*≈100):  B_dep* ≈ 400.0
# Empirical breakeven from the sweep should bracket the mixed-class
# average between med and high (since high-risk dominates expected loss).

# Headline: protocol must enforce B_dep ≥ ~200 USD per insurer
# identity to make Sybil unprofitable across the full risk mix.
# This is the empirical lower bound that closes A5.
